1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eugene Keesey, 73, veteran oilman here and prominent in various local mining operations, died at the family home late Sunday following an extended illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Keesey had lived in the Kellogg area for 32 years and had recently been active in the operation of the Pittsburg silver mine and gold properties in Montana.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Wardner Masonic lodge and Calam temple of the Shrine.
2 CONT
2 CONT His widow, Mae; two sisters, Mrs. Laura Cole and Miss Emma Keesey, both of Eau Claire, Wis., survive.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral rites will be at 3 p. m. Thursday at the McGlade funeral home here with officers of the Wardner Masonic lodge in charge Burial will be in the Kellogg cemetery.
