1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * FT 1801: Deres børn Ugifte: Toten: Dyste
2 CONT
2 CONT Marte Svendsdatter Dyste (1761-1834) married Niels Evensen Gihle Dyste (1752-1836). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Niels took over the farm ”Oppistua” in 1782, and ran it until 1821. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1821 ”Oppistua” was divided into to farms and the other part was called ”Nere”. ”Nere" (the former southern part of "Oppistua") was run by Nils and Marte's son, Christian Nilsen Dyste (1788-1835). ”Oppistua” (the nothern part o
2 CONC f the old "Oppistua") was run by Nils and Martes other son, Even Nilsen Dyste.
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Nilsen Dyste (1788-1835) ran ”Nere” (Dyste søndre) in the years 1821 to 1845. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian married Agnete Hansdatter Lundhagen. When he died of tuberculous she married Peder Alfstad. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Nilsen Dyste's son, Nils Christiansen Dyste (1817-1902), did run ”Nere”, according to the censuse, in 1865. Nils’ three sons, Christian, Mattias og Even, did help their father running the farm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Later Nils’ brother, Hans Christiansen Dyste (1824-1911) took over the farm and ran it until 1888. Why none of his big brother Nils' sons took over is unclear, but it is likely to think that death or moving to Amerika is the reaso
2 CONC n.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Christiansen Dyste married Berte Marie Pedersdatter. In 1888, Hans’ son, Kristian Hansen Dyste (1843-1914), took over, running ”Nere”.
2 CONT
2 CONT ”Nere” (southern Dyste) is a familyfarm since 1678, when Svein Pedersen bought it from Bendik Jørgenssons heirs. In 1396 the name of the farm was written "Diustum".   
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Nielsen Dyste was baptised on the  4th of May 1788.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a caretaker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources/kilder:
2 CONT
2 CONT -Totens bygdebok, Bind 3 (1968), side 598-600.	
2 CONT
2 CONT -1801-telling for 0528 Totens, Digitalarkivet.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Dokument med oversikt over eiere av Dystegårdene gjennom tidene, Dystefamilien.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Gjøvik og Toten slektshistorielag: Gravlagde i Vestre Toten prestegjeld 1825-1837, Digitalpensjonatet, Digitalarkivet.  
2 CONT
2 CONT -Some of the above information was partially provided by Wallace Dyste. He provided dates, however where he had 1855 as the year of Christian Nielsen Dyste's death, I had 1835 (Fred Dyste).
2 CONT
2 CONT -Also I have middle name of Hanson where Wallace has Nilsen. Since his father was Nils, then Nilsen makes more sense. (Fred D.)
2 CONT
2 CONT -In the church book in Norway, his name was written Christian Nielsen. He died of tuberculous. (Hege H.)
