1 NOTE He lived in Minneapolis, MN for 29 years. Ole came to the USA in 1871 and was
2 CONT employed as a miller in the Washburn Crosby Flour Mills.  In 1900 he moved to
2 CONT Mille Lacs County and settled on a farm in Milo Township where lived with his
2 CONT second wife until 1922. They moved to Milaca when he retired. Ole died of a
2 CONT heart attack. His obituary said he was born near Lille Hammer in Norway.
2 CONT Ole's funeral was at the Norweigan Lutheran Church at Milaca.
