1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Utvandret 1871
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sites.google.com/site/totenemigrant/Toten-emigrant-1846/1871-1875
2 CONT
2 CONT Døpt (christened) den 24. februar 1850.
2 CONT
2 CONT Faddere (godparents):
2 CONT
2 CONT Niels Kristiansen Dyste
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Guldbrandsen Dyste
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Andersen Moldestad
2 CONT
2 CONT Karine Christiansdatter Moldestad
2 CONT
2 CONT Berthe Larsdatter Ringen
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1881 John H. Dyste emigrated from Norway to America, at the age of 18. He worked in Eden (now Hudson) S. D., in a store owned by Overseth and Dyste. The Dyste was his oldest brother, Peder (Peter). After a year for which he ear
2 CONC ned the price of a suit, he went to Minneapolis, Minn. to join his brothers Nels and Even, who were working i the market on Washington Ave. In 1885 Nels started a store in Forman (N.D.) and John started one in Rutland (N.D.). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources/kilder:
2 CONT
2 CONT -1865-telling for 0529 Vestre Toten, Digitalarkivet. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -Gjøvik og Toten slektshistorielag: Døypte i Vestre Toten prestegjeld 1850-1855, Digitalpensjonatet, Digitalarkivet. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigrated to the USA with his brothers, but returned to Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Then again maybe he didn't go back. (He was buried in Toten; note T. Kaiser). John Dyste told me there was a feud between Minnesota Dysthe's and North Dakota Dyste's.
2 CONT
2 CONT Today I found a Peter A. Dyste who fits the bill for Per Anton. I will have to renew my subscription to the mormon sites to get more information.
2 CONT
2 CONT Must have returned before 1900, see below.
2 CONT
2 CONT FT 1865: deres Søn ug hjelper Faderen med Gaardsbruget: VT: Dyste
2 CONT
2 CONT FT 1900: hf g Gaardeier, Kristiania kjøpstad: Jacob Aalls Gade 2
2 CONT
2 CONT FT 1910: hf g lever af formue, Kristiania: Jacob Aallsgate 2
