1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * FT 1865: deres Søn ug: VT: Nordnarum østre
2 CONT * FT 1875: søn ug hjælper faderen: VT: NARUM nordre østre
2 CONT * Utvandret 1881 [https://sites.google.com/site/totenemigrant/Toten-emigrant-1846/1881 Link]<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Hansen Narum (arbeider 29 år) f. 19. des. 1851, sønn av Hans Bendixen og Karen Hansdatter Narum nordre. To brødre utvandret senere: Bernt Mauritz, se 1883/140 og Nils, se 1886/27.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans H. Narum. Født paa nordre Narum av forældrene Hans Bendixen og Karen, født Kyseth. Utvandret i 1881. En enkemand, har 1 søn og 2 døtre. Er farmer ved Gary, Minn. (12-p111)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans H. Narum, Pioneer i Green Meadow Township, Gary, Norman County, Minn., døde den 11te December; han manglet bare 9 Dage paa 91 Aar.   Hans H. Narum var født 20de December 1851 i Vestre Toten, Norge, av Forældrene Hans Bendixen
2 CONC  og Karen Narum.  I 1881 reiste han til Amerika og arbeidet en Tid i Nicollet County og senere i Minneapolis.  Den 14de Februar 1885 blev han i Minneapolis gift med Berthe Maria Pederson fra samme Bygd i Norge.  I 1885 reiste han 
2 CONC og hans Hustru til Norman County, hvor de tog Homestead.  Sammen med andre Pionerer stiftet de Gary lutherske Menighed.  Han var meget kirkelig interessert og var i flere Aar Menighedens Sekretær.  Han var den ældste gjenlevende P
2 CONC ioner i Green Meadow Township. Det sidste Aar var han ved daarlig Helbred.    Hans Hustru døde i 1926.   Mr. Narum overleves av en Søn og to Døtre.  Der er fire Barnebarn.  Begravelsen foregik den 16de December fra Gary lutherske 
2 CONC Kirke, Pastor A. O. B. Molldrem forrettet.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Dec. Posten, Aug. 5, 1943)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hans H. Narum, Respected Pioneer Called By Death'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Was one of Early settlers of this community
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans H. Narum died at his home in Green Meadow on Friday evening, December 11th. The cause of his death was infirmity on account of old age. The deceased was born at West Toten, Norway, on December 20th 1851, and he was at the tim
2 CONC e of his death within nine days of being ninety-one years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT He emigrated to this country from his native home in 1881, when he first made his home in Minneapolis, where in 1885 he was united in marriage. Shortly after his marriage he and his wife wended their way to this locality and settl
2 CONC ed in Green Meadow township, where he bought the farm on which he died. This farm he developed and converted from a wild prairie to a fine farm where they lived and prospered.   
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of four children. One son preceded him in death in infancy, and he is survived by the following: Henry Narum, on the home farm; Hilda, who has of late been located in Minneapolis; and Clara (Mrs. Gustav Gjerstad)
2 CONC  of Erskine, this state. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was during his active life industrious and a successful and prosperous farmer and he was always ready and willing to do his fair share of anything that was needed for the locality where he was located. He was active i
2 CONC n church work. He was one of the organizers of the St. Petri congregation, organized in this village, and was doing his fair share in the construction of that church and was always willing to do his share, financially and otherwis
2 CONC e, for the upkeep of the congregation and the church denomination of which he was a member.  He was a good and devoted husband and father, as well as neighbor, and he merited the good will and friendship of all the people he assoc
2 CONC iated with.  He and his family, a few years ago, made their home at Twin Valley, but later sold their home there and moved back on their farm.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife preceded him death a few years ago and after her death he has been making his home with his children, the greater part of the time with his son Henry, who is now the owner of the home farm.  Besides the above children he 
2 CONC is also survived by three grandchildren and as far as it known by one brother in Norway.  In 1927 he was back to his native country, Norway, then he had one brother and two sisters there, but the sisters have later been called by 
2 CONC death. The brother he has not heard from since the war over there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral took place from the home at 12:30 and from the church in this village at 1:30 on Wednesday, the 16th, and the remains were laid to rest in the West cemetery of this congregation.  The bereaved relatives, son and daught
2 CONC ers and other near relatives have a sympathy of their friends in the departure of a father and otherwise relative and friend. (1942) (Ada Historical Society, Norman County, MN)
2 CONT
2 CONT Reiste fra V. Toten. Med “Rollo” 29. apr. Til St. Peter. Frakt kr. 207,60. Medbringende kr. 100. (emi7-p 371)
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial record:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/77270578/hans-narum
